"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIeknGg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T08:47:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T09:34:12Z","body":"> Seems that this code was intentional. This PR basically brings us back to the state before #87006\r\n\r\nIt doesn't, it was `l` and `r` before; it's `left` and `right` now (still resolving the problem).\r\n\r\nThe original PR is a (small) performance hazard in hindsight (making this type not trivially copyable and not `constexpr` compatible) and should not have been merged in the form that it was.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4863895322/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4875828957","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120840#issuecomment-4875828957","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120840","id":4875828957,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIp8-3Q","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T11:52:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T12:05:54Z","body":"I retract the below statement. After talking it through with @Ivorforce it seems obvious that the standard already guarantees for the cases we care about. Thanks for humoring me!\r\n\r\n<details>\r\nLooking at this a bit more (because I was reviewing #120845), I think maybe we should add one more static assert to this (And all of the changes in #120845) It is perhaps super pedantic, but what else am I here for:\r\n\r\n```\r\nstatic_assert(alignof(AudioFrame) >= alignof(float));\r\n```\r\n\r\nLike, in practice I don't think there's really any case where this can't hold, but if we're doing the static asserts anyway...\r\n</details>","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4875828957/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4875948370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120840#issuecomment-4875948370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120840","id":4875948370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIqERUg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T12:06:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T12:06:37Z","body":"We resolved the above comment in chat. Practically, the guarantee follows from the \"first member is at offset 0\" guarantee + the \"every member is placed at its correct alignment\" guarantee. This can only hold if the owning struct's alignment is at least that of each of its fields.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4875948370/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4877500548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120840#issuecomment-487750